# What is checked mechanically

After you publish, every map-stage gate runs again on your branch, plus the
`trace` gate; a failed gate discards the branch:

- `corpus_untouched`: no change under `{{ corpus_root }}`.
- `lint`: `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass on every Python file
  the branch touches.
- `paths`: every commit touches only what its kind allows; a `[REVIEW]`
  commit that touches the implementation fails here.
- `no_changelog`: no file under any `changelog/` directory is added or
  changed. Never write a changelog entry; the annealer writes them.
- `units_reported`: the outcome's coordinates are exactly the units above.
- `links`: `{{ witness_links_filename }}` is present, no link is broken, and
  every unit with a verdict other than `NONE` has at least one link.
- `junit`: `{{ junit_filename }}` is present, has no failure or error, and
  every node id in your trace is present and passed.
- `trace`: every traced clause is one of the unit's clauses; every traced
  assertion string occurs in the named test's source at the branch tip; a
  `FULL` unit traces every clause and lists no open-world clause; a
  `PARTIAL_STEADY` unit traces every clause it does not list as open-world.

